# Trait Doctoring's "target permanent" (CR 115.1, 110.1): neither a player nor a card in a hand can be its target, where
# Artificial Evolution's "target spell or permanent" (artificial-evolution-targets-a-spell-or-a-permanent-and-nothing-else)
# names a spell as well. A spell can never be Trait Doctoring's target in a game: it is a sorcery, cast with an empty
# stack, and so is the copy that cipher casts as it resolves. A permanent that can't be targeted (hexproof, CR 702.11b), Bot2's
# Sylvan Caryatid, is refused too. The positive control is the same cast at Bot1's Forest, which is offered where those are not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Island
Trait Doctoring
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Sylvan Caryatid
Mountain
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sylvan Caryatid.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
? Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Jet; Sylvan Caryatid
! Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Bot2)
! Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Bot2.Hand.Mountain)
! Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid)
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a basic land type)
Bot1.Modes(Forest)
Bot1.Modes(Island)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Subtypes = Island

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Trait Doctoring
